 ### [Viewing Plane Ray Generation](2424-viewing-plane-ray-generation.md)
-Viewing Plane Ray Generation constructs the initial rays for volume rendering by defining a projection plane parallel to the scanline and casting rays in the viewing direction within that plane. It serves as the geometric foundation for orthographic ray casting, where ray origins are distributed across a 2D grid and all rays share a single normalized direction. This method generates parallel rays, contrasting with perspective ray generation which supports non-parallel viewing.
+Viewing Plane Ray Generation constructs the initial rays for volume rendering by defining a projection plane parallel to the scanline and casting rays in the viewing direction within that plane. It serves as the geometric foundation for orthographic ray casting, where ray origins are distributed across a 2D grid and all rays share a single normalized direction. It generates parallel rays, contrasting with perspective ray generation which supports non-parallel viewing. Choose it when metric-preserving, distortion-free projection is required.
 
 ### [Orthographic Projection](4019-orthographic-projection.md)
-A size-preserving projection where objects in the foreground take up the same amount of screen space as objects in the background, and parallel lines in the 3D scene remain parallel when drawn on the screen.
+Orthographic Projection is a size-preserving projection where objects in the foreground take up the same amount of screen space as objects in the background, and parallel lines in the 3D scene remain parallel when drawn on the screen. Choose it for technical drawings, CAD, and scientific visualizations where accurate spatial relationships are critical.
 
 ### Orthographic Camera Handling for Point Clouds
